A||||7||V8Fiero||Trouble w/ axles after V8 swap??||||8||
Z||000000||V8Fiero||07-25-2000||10:27 PM||||Hi all,<P> Just curious if any of you that have done the V8 swap have had trouble with the length of the two axles. I used the archie kit. I had trouble with the passenger side axle coming out of the transmission (auto). Called Archie on that one and he said that a bad alignment would cause that. I did have that axle lengthened to be safe because it looked like the cv joints were borderline. Just the opposite happened on the driver side. Because the whole engine/trans assembly moved to the driver side, now that axle is too long. Looks like the cv joint is pushed together and I am having trouble getting the alignment back to specs. Havent taken the axle to see if they can shorten it yet.<P>Sorry to be so long winded. Just curious if Im the only one that this happened to or if there are others.<P>Thanks.||||reg||8
Z||000001||Rodney||07-25-2000||10:46 PM||||Try an axle and driveshaft shop. There are many GM axles in many different lenghts. The CV ends change but a lot of axles have the same splines. They should have a listing of all the lenghts available. If you know what you need they may have it. <P>Rodney Dickman||||reg||1
Z||000002||HarryG||07-26-2000||03:20 PM||||You had the axle lengthened?  I've heard of axles being shortened, but not lengthened. Or did you use another longer unit?<P>Also curious what you found out from the axle shop that Rodney mentioned. ||||reg||5
Z||000003||batboy||07-26-2000||06:47 PM||||Sounds like you didn't get the engine centered in the correct place. I've had no problems with my axles. When I was doing my suspension rebuild, I found one bad CV boot and it seemed the CV joints had a little wear, so I replaced both drive axles. I've put over 6k miles on with no problems...they fit perfect.||||reg||1
Z||000004||V8Fiero||07-26-2000||06:54 PM||||I had a machine shop that specialized in drivelines lenghten one (he cut it and put a sleeve over it and welded it together) its pretty much bulletproof. However I am now over 400 miles from that shop.<P>Batboy:<P>I dont see how I couldve gotten the engine anymore centered. My harmonic balancer pulley is just barely clearing the frame. And that is the side that was too short. <P>I havent tried yet to find a shop to either fabricate an axle or to find a GM replacement yet. Was just curious of some other peoples findings on this subject.<BR>Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Richard Parnell||07-27-2000||04:01 PM||||Now I am confused.  One of the more attractive features of the Archie kit to me is that you don't have to alter the length of the axles.  Althought the pulley does extend into the wheel well a bit I'm willing to go with it, just to have a rocket.  But back to the axle lengths , I would like to confirm that the axle lengths stay the same as it states in the proceedures on Archies' site.  Any info would be helpful guys.  Thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000006||batboy||07-27-2000||08:25 PM||||V8Fiero, what SBC do you have and what year? There are three 8" production balancers, one of which is thinner (has a 1-5/16" inertia ring) than the other two. This is original equipment on 69 Z-28 302 engines (p/n 3947708) Another damper (p/n 6272221) is only 6-3/4" in diameter and used on many 69 and newer 305's and 350's. Maybe a thinner or a smaller diameter balancer would work better. Info found in the Chevrolet Power book.||||reg||1
Z||000007||V8Fiero||07-27-2000||11:13 PM||||First of all the engine I used was a 1975 350 out of a Chev. Caprice. My first mistake was to disconnect the struts from the spindles. I think if I didnt do this I wouldnt have a problem. Maybe the yr of engine that I used there was no way to escape this. Although the minor problems that I have encountered, I would have never, and I mean never, would have bought anyone else's kit other than Archies. I have called him, emailed him, and have never gotten anything than useful info. I think my problem is probably my fault and not the kits. Be sure to read and research before you spend X amount of dollars and know what you are getting into.<P>Scott||||reg||1
